    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.operators / replace operator\n\n### Description\n\nGiven this example:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal foo = {\r\n\t\"apple\",\r\n\t\"orange\",\r\n\t\"banana\"\r\n}\r\nbuySome(fruits)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI yank \"banana\" with `yy`, go two lines down, and want to substitute `fruits` via `grib`.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- result includes the leading whitespace\r\nbuySome(\t\"banana\")\r\n\r\n-- expected/desired result\r\nbuySome(\"banana\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nI cannot really think of a scenario where the current behavior would be desirable, so I would like to propose to change the replace-operation to trim text when replacing a charwise object with linewise content.",
